WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:06.680
In Season 6 of Game of Thrones – and hopefully
soon in the books – Daenerys Targaryen sails

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:12.549
west, hoping to take the Throne of Westeros.
She brings with her an army, and a navy, and

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:17.411
three dragons – but her war won’t be easy.
If Dany’s to succeed in her conquest, she

00:00:17.411 --> 00:00:21.810
should take some lessons from Game of Thrones
history – because this is actually the second

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:27.850
time a Targaryen has invaded Westeros from
the east with three dragons. The first time

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:33.020
was three hundred years ago, in the Conquest
of Aegon Targaryen.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:39.440
So before Tommen and Joffrey and Robert Baratheon,
the King of Westeros was Aerys Targaryen,

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:45.420
the father of Daenerys and Viserys. Before
Aerys was a dozen generations of Targaryen

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.950
kings, a dynasty of three centuries, which
was founded by Aegon Targaryen. Aegon’s

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:56.380
family originally came from Valyria, the empire
of the dragonlords, but it blew up – which

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:02.710
is kind of its own story. The Targaryens escaped
this Doom and settled on Dragonstone, an island

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:07.360
just off Westeros, and for generations they
stayed there, trading in the Narrow Sea , and

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.610
meddling in eastern politics, but when Aegon
became Lord of Dragonstone, his interest was

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.290
Westeros .
Westeros, at the time, was divided into seven

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:22.140
Kingdoms – the north was ruled by King Torrhen
Stark, the Vale by Queen Regent Sharra Arryn

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.000
for her young son Ronnel, the Iron Islands
and the riverlands ruled by King Harren Hoare,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.100
the westerlands ruled by King Loren Lannister,
the Reach by King Mern Gardener, the stormlands

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:38.110
by King Argilac Durrandon, and Dorne by Princess
Meria Martell. These kingdoms had been fighting

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:43.530
one another for centuries, but the way Aegon
saw it, Westeros was “One realm, for one

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:48.409
king to rule alone” . He was to be that
king – so he planned an invasion.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:54.650
We don’t know much about Aegon as a person.
He was a great warrior and leader, but also

00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:00.040
an “enigma” – reserved, with few friends
. His closest companions were his sisters

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:06.110
– who were also his wives, cause the Targaryens
really love incest – Visenya and Rhaenys.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:11.890
Visenya was a skilled warrior, stern and serious
, while Rhaenys was more playful and impulsive,

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:17.800
a lover of music and dancing . There was also
Orys Baratheon, Aegon’s friend and possibly

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:23.580
his bastard half-brother . The Targaryens
had alliances with Houses Bar Emmon, Celtigar,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.340
Massey and Velaryon , all minor houses that
were based nearby to Dragonstone. And the

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.890
Targaryens also had dragons – Visenya rode
a dragon called Vhagar, Rhaenys rode a dragon

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:40.250
called Meraxes, and Aegon rode a monster called
Balerion, the Black Dread, a dragon so huge

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:44.390
“that whole towns were swallowed up” in
the shadow of his wings when he passed over

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.080
them . After the destruction of Valyria, these
three were the only dragons known to exist

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:54.840
in the world. So that was team Targaryen at
the beginning of the Conquest – Aegon, his

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:00.960
sisters, and their three dragons, Orys Baratheon,
the Bar Emmons, Celtigars, Masseys and Velaryons.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.629
They raised a small army and landed on Westeros.
At the place where they landed, the mouth

00:03:06.629 --> 00:03:12.330
of the Blackwater river, Aegon built a small
fort, the Aegonfort. Rhaenys and Visenya went

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:16.379
and took over the nearby small castles of
Stokeworth and Rosby – which was pretty

00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:21.720
easy because they had dragons. The lords of
Duskendale and Maidenpool gathered an army,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.220
and marched on Aegon with three thousand men,
but Aegon easily destroyed them with his dragon

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.349
– if you pay close attention you might start
to see a pattern here. Then back at the Aegonfort,

00:03:31.349 --> 00:03:35.989
they had a ceremony where Aegon let his defeated
enemies keep their old lands and positions

00:03:35.989 --> 00:03:42.170
– so long as they joined his side. Visenya
crowned Aegon, Rhaenys named him King of Westeros,

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:47.630
and they unfurled a Targaryen banner – a
red three-headed dragon on black silk. The

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:52.560
Targaryens and their Valyrian ancestors didn’t
have a tradition of heraldry, but Aegon used

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:57.870
this Westerosi custom as way of showing he
was one of them. When the lords saw Aegon’s

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:02.720
banner, they took at as a sign that he was
a worthy high king for Westeros . But there

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.220
was still some conquering left to do.
One of Aegon’s first moves was to send a

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:13.050
fleet of ships led by Daemon Velaryon to attack
Gulltown and the Vale of Arryn. The Arryns

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:17.239
got a fleet together and managed to beat the
Targaryens, sinking a third of their ships,

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:22.220
and killing Daemon Velaryon. But in response,
Visenya came and burned the Vale’s fleet

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:27.020
with her dragon, Vhagar. This kinda sets the
tone for the rest of the Conquest – sometimes

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.949
the Targaryens did get beat, but never for
long, because in the end, “Aegon’s enemies

00:04:31.949 --> 00:04:37.020
had no answer for his dragons” . Well, except
for Dorne – but we’re getting ahead of

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.939
ourselves.
Aegon marched on to his first real challenge

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:45.159
– King Harren Hoare. House Hoare was originally
from the Iron Islands, but they came to rule

00:04:45.159 --> 00:04:50.110
the riverlands as well. Harren was called
“the Black”, and was legendary for his

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:55.360
cruelty . He built a tremendous castle called
Harrenhal, and made the riverlanders pay for

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.349
it , plundering from the local lords, and
working thousands of people to death . As

00:05:00.349 --> 00:05:05.189
Aegon approached Harrenhal with his army,
he was attacked by Harren’s men twice. In

00:05:05.189 --> 00:05:09.439
the second battle, two of Harren’s sons
managed to sneak up and kill a bunch of Aegon’s

00:05:09.439 --> 00:05:13.909
men in the night, but in the morning, Aegon
burned Harren’s sons with his dragon as

00:05:13.909 --> 00:05:18.349
they tried to escape across a lake. Harren
tried to rally the riverlords to help him

00:05:18.349 --> 00:05:22.929
fight, but instead, they rose up against him,
under the leadership of a Lord Edmyn Tully

00:05:22.929 --> 00:05:28.900
. Suddenly outnumbered, Harren retreated to
his castle. When Aegon came, he offered Harren

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.610
peace, said if he gave up, he’d let him
go home to the Iron Islands. He said he had

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:38.399
eight thousand men outside Harren’s walls.
Harren said what’s outside of his walls

00:05:38.399 --> 00:05:44.740
if of no concern, because his walls are strong
and thick. Aegon said but I have dragons,

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:51.409
dragons fly. Harren said stone doesn’t burn.
So Aegon said when the sun sets your line

00:05:51.409 --> 00:05:57.020
shall end. When night fell, Aegon descended
on Harrenhal with his dragon, bathing its

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:02.069
towers in fire until they began to melt like
candles – everything inside was caught on

00:06:02.069 --> 00:06:08.059
fire – wood and wool, hemp and straw, and
all of Harren’s men. The greatest castle

00:06:08.059 --> 00:06:13.779
in Westeros was made a ruin that night, and
Harren died along with his entire line. In

00:06:13.779 --> 00:06:18.000
the morning, the riverlords pledged their
allegiance to Aegon, and Edmyn Tully was named

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.809
Lord Paramount of the Trident – the ancestor
of Hoster, Brynden, Catelyn, Lysa and Edmure.

00:06:23.809 --> 00:06:29.059
As for Harrenhal, its twisted melted ruins
are now believed to be cursed – almost every

00:06:29.059 --> 00:06:33.029
character who holds Harrenhal in the main
story so far has ended up violently murdered

00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:36.560
one way or another – Littlefinger and Roose
Bolton in the books are two of the only ones

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:42.529
to survive – so far. But yeah, Aegon defeated
Harren Hoare and took the riverlands. The

00:06:42.529 --> 00:06:46.770
Iron Islands Aegon kind of ignored for a few
years, but later he came and sorted them out

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:51.339
and allowed them to pick their own leader.
They chose Vickon Greyjoy – ancestor of

00:06:51.339 --> 00:06:56.120
Balon, Euron, Aeron, Asha – or Yara – and
Theon.

00:06:56.120 --> 00:07:00.339
While Aegon took the riverlands, Rhaenys and
Orys went to take the stormlands. On their

00:07:00.339 --> 00:07:04.099
way to the castle of Storm’s End, they were
ambushed by Argilac’s men, who killed a

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:09.629
thousand Targaryen soldiers before melting
back into the forests. So Rhaenys burned the

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:14.809
forests, killed the men, and kept on marching.
By now, King Argilac had heard what had happened

00:07:14.809 --> 00:07:19.740
to Harren, so he decided to leave his castle
and attack the Targaryens in the field. From

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:24.740
dragonback Rhaenys saw them coming, so she
and Orys and the Targaryen army dug in and

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:30.709
waited for them come. Right on cue, a huge,
dramatic storm began, a steady rain became

00:07:30.709 --> 00:07:36.640
a howling gale, setting the stage for a massive
battle later called the Last Storm. Because

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.870
of the storm, Rhaenys’ dragon Meraxes couldn’t
fly, so the battle was actually a pretty fair

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:46.490
fight. It raged well into the night , with
Argilac charging the Targaryens with cavalry

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:51.379
and spearmen, until finally he broke though
to his enemies’ centre, and was faced with

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:56.999
Rhaenys and Meraxes. The dragon burned Argilac’s
best men and scattered his cavalry, and Argilac

00:07:56.999 --> 00:08:02.669
was killed in single combat with Orys Baratheon.
The battle ended, and after a brief resistance

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:07.659
by Argilac’s daughter, Argella, the stormlands
were won for Aegon. Orys married Argella,

00:08:07.659 --> 00:08:12.860
and took the Durrandon castle, sigil and house
words for his own – and so the house Baratheon

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:19.520
was founded , ancestors of Robert, Stannis,
Renly, and don’t forget, Robert’s bastard

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:22.080
Gendry.
On the other side of Westeros, the Kings of

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.569
the westerlands and the reach – Loren Lannister
and Mern Gardener – decided that enough

00:08:26.569 --> 00:08:31.860
was enough . They raised the biggest army
ever seen in Westeros, over fifty thousand

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:37.560
strong, and marched on the Targaryens. Aegon,
with his much smaller army, came to meet them,

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:43.159
and they clashed in a field of wheat and grass,
which Aegon noted was very dry, it hadn’t

00:08:43.159 --> 00:08:47.720
rained in while. The battle began, blokes
started killing blokes but then the Targaryens

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:52.880
activated their trap card – which was–
it was– it was their dragons. Rhaenys and

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.959
Visenya started big fires to the sides and
behind the enemy, trapping them, while Balerion

00:08:57.959 --> 00:09:03.250
filled the enemy lines with flame and smoke.
Thousands of men were burned alive in what

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:08.910
was later called the Field of Fire . King
Loren Lannister managed to escape. He surrendered

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:14.160
to Aegon, and was made Warden of the West,
ancestor to Tywin, Tyrion, Cersei, and Jaime.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.150
But King Mern and his family were all wiped
out, ending House Gardener, who had ruled

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:24.790
the reach for thousands of years. Control
of the reach then fell to Harlen of House

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:29.240
Tyrell, who had served the Gardeners as stewards
for many years. Harlen immediately surrendered

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:34.300
to Aegon, and so was given dominion over the
reach as Aegon’s Warden of the South . Interestingly,

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:39.600
it’s implied, at least in the Blu-ray features
for the show, that it was the Tyrells' idea

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:44.410
for the Gardeners to go get themselves killed
so that the Tyrells could take over – these

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:49.509
schemers are ancestors of Margaery, Mace and
Loras.

00:09:49.509 --> 00:09:53.220
After the reach and westerlands were conquered,
Aegon heard the northmen were on the march,

00:09:53.220 --> 00:09:58.959
so he rushed up with all his army to meet
King Torrhen Stark. Torrhen had a pretty big

00:09:58.959 --> 00:10:03.740
army, with thirty thousand northmen, but he
saw that Aegon’s was bigger, a huge host

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:08.660
of riverlanders, stormlanders, westerlanders,
reachmen, everyone he had conquered and won

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:13.690
over to his side. Torrhen saw Aegon’s dragons,
and heard how they burned thousands on the

00:10:13.690 --> 00:10:18.420
Field of Fire, and at Harrenhal. And Torrhen
thought – do we really wanna fight these

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:23.480
guys? Some of his bannermen wanted to attack,
others wanted to fall back to Moat Cailin,

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:28.100
Torrhen’s “bastard brother Brandon Snow
offered to” sneak into Aegon’s camp and

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:34.360
kill his dragons. But in the end Torrhen decided
to make peace. He knelt, gave up his crown,

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:39.350
and swore the north to Aegon. Forever after
Torrhen was known as the King Who Knelt, and

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:44.199
his Stark descendants were no longer Kings
of Winter, but only Wardens of the North.

00:10:44.199 --> 00:10:48.080
Some northmen were angry that their king would
surrender, but it’s hard to deny Torrhen

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:53.899
saved the north from a war they probably wouldn’t
have won. Still – this Brandon Snow thing

00:10:53.899 --> 00:10:58.330
is interesting. Torrhen’s brother offered
to “cross the Trident alone under cover

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:04.500
of darkness, to slay [Aegon’s] dragons [while]
they slept”. Was this guy brave or stupid?

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:09.129
Did he have a plan to kill these dragons?
There is a bit in Dance that could give a

00:11:09.129 --> 00:11:14.220
hint of what Brandon was thinking. Bran Stark
has a vision of the distant past where he

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:19.290
sees a pale, fierce youth in the Winterfell
godswood, slicing three branches of weirwood

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:24.850
off the heart tree and shaping them into arrows.
Some fans believe that that youth is Brandon

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:30.529
Snow, and speculate that those three weirwood
arrows could have had some power to kill Aegon’s

00:11:30.529 --> 00:11:35.000
three dragons – weirwood is linked to the
magic of the old gods and the children of

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:39.619
the forest. So, there isn’t much to go on
here, but it is an interesting possibility

00:11:39.619 --> 00:11:44.970
– maybe dragon-killing weirwood arrows will
come back into the story at some point.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:49.981
In the Vale, Queen Regent Sharra Arryn had
just seen five of Westeros’ seven kingdoms

00:11:49.981 --> 00:11:55.709
fall to Aegon – so she raised her defences.
She put a strong army at the Bloody Gate,

00:11:55.709 --> 00:12:00.939
and garrisons all up the Eyrie – the reputedly
impregnable castle of the Arryn Kings . But

00:12:00.939 --> 00:12:05.329
all her defences turned out to be useless
when Visenya flew over them on dragonback,

00:12:05.329 --> 00:12:09.769
easily landing in the Eyrie’s inner courtyard
. When Queen Sharra ran out to face her with

00:12:09.769 --> 00:12:14.100
her guards, she found her son Ronnel sitting
on Visenya’s knee, asking for a ride on

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:19.649
the dragon. In the end, Sharra and Visenya
had a nice chat, Ronnel got a ride on a dragon,

00:12:19.649 --> 00:12:24.499
and when he landed, he was no longer a little
king, but a little lord . The Vale yielded

00:12:24.499 --> 00:12:29.860
to Aegon, and joined his realm.
After the Vale, there was one kingdom left

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:35.760
to conquer. Rhaenys mounted her dragon Meraxes,
and flew out to the sands of Dorne. She came

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:40.449
to the castle of Vaith, and flew down to take
it, but it was empty – none of the lords

00:12:40.449 --> 00:12:44.730
or guards were there, and the peasants wouldn’t
say where they went. So Rhaenys flew onto

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:49.449
Godsgrace, then Planky Town, but could find
only women and children. Finally she came

00:12:49.449 --> 00:12:54.689
to Sunspear, home of the Martell Princes of
Dorne, and found it too abandoned except for

00:12:54.689 --> 00:13:01.009
the Princess of Dorne herself, Meria Martell.
Meria was old and fat and blind – some called

00:13:01.009 --> 00:13:06.129
her the “Yellow Toad of Dorne” – but
she was still very sharp. Meria told Rhaenys

00:13:06.129 --> 00:13:11.170
that she wouldn’t fight, but she wouldn’t
kneel – that the Martell house words are

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:16.139
“Unbowed, Unbent, Unbroken”. She said
that Dorne has no king, that Rhaenys isn’t

00:13:16.139 --> 00:13:22.740
wanted in Dorne, to return at her peril. So,
Rhaenys left – “and Dorne remained unconquered”.

00:13:22.740 --> 00:13:27.439
Rhaenys did come back in another Targaryen
attack ten years later, and when she did,

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:32.530
Rhaenys was killed. A scorpion bolt pierced
Meraxes’ eye, and the dragon and the queen

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:38.269
fell from the sky . Every time the Targaryens
tried to take Dorne, Dorne beat them, by using

00:13:38.269 --> 00:13:42.520
these guerilla tactics. Whenever the dragons
came, the Dornish wouldn’t line up to be

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:48.329
roasted like at the Field of Fire, they would
“vanish”. Melt away, leaving “only stone

00:13:48.329 --> 00:13:52.600
and sand for them to burn” , emerging when
it was safe to kill their enemies from the

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:57.649
shadows. It wasn’t til over a hundred years
later that Dorne finally joined the Seven

00:13:57.649 --> 00:14:02.350
Kingdoms, and even then it wasn’t by conquest
but by diplomacy and marriage – Dorne joined

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:08.070
Westeros on their own terms – an attitude
upheld by some of Meria’s ancestors – including

00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:14.470
Oberyn, Doran, Elia and Trystane.
So Aegon failed to conquer Dorne, but six

00:14:14.470 --> 00:14:18.889
out of seven kingdoms ain't bad. He came to
Oldtown, the biggest city in Westeros, and

00:14:18.889 --> 00:14:23.829
the centre of the Faith of the Seven , which
is like the Catholic Church of Game of Thrones.

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:28.459
The High Septon, kind of the Pope, had spent
seven days and seven nights praying to the

00:14:28.459 --> 00:14:33.370
gods for advice on Aegon, and eventually he
decided that he would not fight the guy with

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:37.529
the dragons who just conquered most of the
country, but would declare him the rightful

00:14:37.529 --> 00:14:42.189
ruler. So the Septon “anointed Aegon with
… seven oils, placed a crown upon his head,

00:14:42.189 --> 00:14:46.899
and proclaimed him Aegon of House Targaryen,
the First of His Name, King of the Andals,

00:14:46.899 --> 00:14:51.810
the Rhoynar, and the First Men, Lord of the
Seven Kingdoms, and Protector of the Realm”

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:55.579
. Aegon decided to rule his great new realm
from the new town that was growing round the

00:14:55.579 --> 00:15:00.660
Aegonfort, which eventually would become the
city of King’s Landing. Aegon made a throne

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:05.990
out of the swords of his defeated enemies,
the Iron Throne, which looks way cooler in

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:10.050
the books.
So that is how Aegon conquered Westeros – what

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:15.690
can Daenerys learn from this? The first, most
obvious lesson is that her most valuable assets

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:21.649
are her dragons. She can use them to destroy
enemy castles and armies and fleets, to control

00:15:21.649 --> 00:15:26.240
battlefields, to scout ahead, to intimidate
– they’ll probably be very useful against

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:32.930
the white walkers – but Dany will also have
to protect her dragons – they can be killed.

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:37.190
As Rhaenys learned in Dorne, a scorpion bolt
can kill one . And historically they’ve

00:15:37.190 --> 00:15:41.860
also been killed by arrows, even by mobs of
angry peasants, if they get trapped indoors

00:15:41.860 --> 00:15:47.529
. There might also be the risk of somehow
losing control of one of her dragons. In the

00:15:47.529 --> 00:15:53.050
books, Euron Greyjoy has a magic horn that
he claims can “bind dragons to [his] will”

00:15:53.050 --> 00:15:57.389
. There’s also speculation that Bran or
the Night King could do some skinchanging

00:15:57.389 --> 00:16:02.269
magic shenanigans to take one of Dany’s
dragons, just like Bran wargs Hodor, and the

00:16:02.269 --> 00:16:06.920
walkers control wights. Basically, there’re
a lot of things that could go wrong with the

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:11.170
dragons, and honestly, Dany’ll probably
lose at least one of them somehow – the

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:15.860
story’d be boring if she just easily won
with them, right? Also, Dany should watch

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:20.779
out for guerrilla tactics like the Targaryens
faced in Dorne. She’s already come up against

00:16:20.779 --> 00:16:25.240
this sort of thing with the Sons of the Harpy
in Meereen, who hide in the day, and strike

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:29.860
at night , and Dany wasn’t much good at
dealing with these guys. The basic problem

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:34.300
is that dragons are great at killing your
enemies, but only if you know who your enemies

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:39.529
are and where your enemies are. And sadly,
in the game of thrones, things aren’t always

00:16:39.529 --> 00:16:42.980
so straightforward.
Something else Dany might wanna think about

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:49.189
is political and cultural legitimacy. Aegon
was really smart in using symbols and traditions

00:16:49.189 --> 00:16:53.829
that showed he’d be a worthy ruler, that
he would rule not as some Valyrian foreign

00:16:53.829 --> 00:16:59.410
overlord, but as a Westerosi king. He used
Westerosi heraldry, he was anointed by the

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:05.539
leader of Westerosi religion, and he built
a huge visible tangible symbol of his political

00:17:05.539 --> 00:17:10.970
power in the Iron Throne, using the actual
swords of his enemies to embody his right

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:15.410
of conquest. All these things contributed
to Aegon’s legitimacy in the eyes of the

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:20.220
people he ruled, to make him the sort of leader
that people were happy to follow. Dany should

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:25.010
consider this stuff too. She’s spent almost
all her life far from Westeros, and she leads

00:17:25.010 --> 00:17:29.850
a mostly foreign army – so there’s a risk
that people will see her not as a rightful

00:17:29.850 --> 00:17:34.560
queen, but as a foreign conqueror. One easy
way to improve this is to remind everyone,

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:40.779
as she often does, that she is the blood of
Valyria, a descendent of Aegon , and the inheritor

00:17:40.779 --> 00:17:46.340
of his dynasty. She might not wanna remind
people, however, that her father was the notoriously

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:51.200
cruel and crazy “Mad King”, who Robert
fought a rebellion to usurp. So – might

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:56.720
wanna be sensitive there. Another interesting
issue for Dany is religion. Dany seems to

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:00.910
have no interest in the Faith of the Seven,
and besides, the High Septon just got blown

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:06.120
up in the show, so the Faith’s probably
in disarray anyway. But Dany is making connections

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:11.100
to the Red God, the Lord of Light, she’s
rubbing shoulders with red priests, who claim

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:15.820
she’s Azor Ahai. This might help get her
support in Essos, but most Westerosi don’t

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:20.600
follow the Red God, so this could actually
work against her – she’ll wanna be careful

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:24.710
there.
Finally, part of what made Aegon successful

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:29.380
was that he didn’t just destroy all his
enemies with dragonfire. He always offered

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:34.419
mercy – so long as foes bent the knee, he’d
even let them keep their lands and titles

00:18:34.419 --> 00:18:40.600
. Aegon turned his enemies into allies, Robert
Baratheon did the same thing. But will Daenerys

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:46.260
be so merciful? She’s been pretty burny
lately , more fire and blood than peace and

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:50.870
diplomacy . In the show she talks about “breaking
the wheel”, destroying the great houses

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:55.960
of Westeros rather than winning them to her
side. “Aegon the Conqueror brought fire

00:18:55.960 --> 00:19:01.091
and blood to Westeros, but afterward he gave
them peace, prosperity, and justice”. Will

00:19:01.091 --> 00:19:07.919
Dany do the same? Or will she bring only “death
and ruin”? We’ll have to wait and see.

